---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import LegalTabs from '../components/LegalTabs.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use (EULA) — Odys Travel"
  description="Terms of Use and EULA for Odys Travel, including Apple Standard EULA, licenses, and subscriptions."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <div class="odys-card p-8 sm:p-12">
      <a href="/odys/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold text-[#FF7A59] mb-6 hover:underline">
        ← Back to Odys Travel
      </a>
      <LegalTabs active="terms" />

      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold text-[#FF7A59] uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
        <span>Standard Apple EULA &amp; Developer Terms · Effective November 4, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-4">Terms of Use (EULA) for Odys Travel</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#6A647E] dark:text-[#928C9D] mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-black/5 dark:border-white/5 space-y-1">
        <span class="block"><strong class="text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA]">Effective Date:</strong> November 4, 2026</span>
        <span class="block"><strong class="text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA]">Developer:</strong> Dmitry Sinkevich</span>
        <span class="block"><strong class="text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA]">Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:dmitry8.work@gmail.com" class="text-[#FF7A59] underline">dmitry8.work@gmail.com</a></span>
      </p>

      <div class="legal-prose space-y-8 text-sm text-[#6A647E] dark:text-[#928C9D] leading-relaxed">
        <p class="mb-3">
          These Terms of Use (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of the Odys Travel iOS application (“the App”). By downloading, installing, accessing, or using the App, you agree to these Terms and to Apple’s standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement (“Apple Standard EULA”).
        </p>
        <p>
          If you do not agree to these Terms, do not download, install, or use the App.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">1. Apple Standard EULA</h2>
          <p>
            Your use of the App is also subject to Apple’s standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement. In the event of a conflict between these Terms and the Apple Standard EULA, the Apple Standard EULA controls with respect to matters governed by Apple.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">2. License to Use the App</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Subject to your compliance with these Terms, Dmitry Sinkevich grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to download, install, and use the App on Apple devices that you own or control, solely for personal, non-commercial use.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">You may not:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>Copy, modify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works from the App.</li>
            <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to derive the source code of the App, except where permitted by applicable law.</li>
            <li>Rent, lease, lend, sell, redistribute, or sublicense the App.</li>
            <li>Remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, trademark, or proprietary notices in the App.</li>
            <li>Use the App for any unlawful purpose or in any way that could damage, disable, overburden, or impair the App.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">3. Nature of the App</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Odys Travel is a personal visual journaling and travel-exploration tool. It helps you organize travel memories, view countries and cities associated with photo timestamps and location metadata, and explore an approximate visual map of your travels.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Country counts, stay durations, routes, distances, and related statistics are estimates based on available photo metadata, user-entered information, and approximate geographic boundaries.
          </p>
          <p>
            Odys Travel is not intended for legal immigration tracking, tax-residency determination, visa compliance, official border-control purposes, or any other legally binding use. Do not rely on the App as evidence of your presence, residence, immigration status, or compliance with any law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">4. Geographic Information and Map Data</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Country borders, regional boundaries, and related geographic data are adapted from Natural Earth, which is in the public domain.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            City coordinates and place-related information may be derived from GeoNames, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License.
          </p>
          <p>
            Geographic boundaries, place names, and political representations may be approximate, incomplete, outdated, or subject to dispute. Odys Travel aims to present geographic information neutrally and does not endorse any position regarding disputed territories or borders.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">5. User Content</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            “User Content” means trips, notes, photos, photo metadata, locations, countries, cities, tags, favorites, settings, and other content that you create, import, or store using the App.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            You retain all rights that you hold in your User Content. By using the App, you grant Dmitry Sinkevich only the limited permission necessary to store, process, and display your User Content locally on your device in order to provide the App’s features.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Odys Travel is designed to process User Content locally on your device. We do not claim ownership of your User Content.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are responsible for maintaining backups of your User Content. Uninstalling the App, resetting your device, losing access to your device, or deleting App data may result in permanent loss of locally stored User Content.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">6. Acceptable Use</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">You agree not to use the App to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>Violate applicable laws, regulations, or third-party rights.</li>
            <li>Upload, import, or distribute content that is unlawful, harmful, threatening, abusive, harassing, defamatory, obscene, or otherwise objectionable.</li>
            <li>Infringe the intellectual-property, privacy, publicity, or contractual rights of any person.</li>
            <li>Interfere with the operation of the App or attempt to gain unauthorized access to any system or data.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">7. In-App Purchases and Subscriptions</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Certain features of the App may be available through a one-time purchase, lifetime unlock, or auto-renewing subscription processed by Apple through the App Store.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            All purchases, payments, renewals, cancellations, refunds, and billing-related matters are managed through your Apple ID and Apple’s App Store payment system. We do not collect or store your payment-card details.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">If you purchase an auto-renewing subscription:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mb-3">
            <li>Payment will be charged to your Apple ID account at confirmation of purchase.</li>
            <li>Your subscription automatically renews unless auto-renewal is turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.</li>
            <li>Your account will be charged for renewal within 24 hours before the end of the current period.</li>
            <li>You can manage or cancel your subscription in your device Settings by going to <strong class="text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA]">Settings &gt; your name &gt; Subscriptions</strong>.</li>
            <li>If you cancel, your subscription remains active until the end of the current paid period.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The name, length, price, and features included in each subscription or one-time purchase are displayed in the App before you complete the purchase. Prices may vary by region and are determined by Apple and applicable taxes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">8. Refunds</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Purchases and subscriptions are processed by Apple. Refund requests should be submitted through Apple’s report-a-problem process or by contacting Apple Support.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not have the ability to issue direct refunds for purchases made through the App Store.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">9. Restore Purchases</h2>
          <p>
            If you reinstall the App, switch to a new device, or sign in with the same Apple ID, you may be able to restore eligible previous purchases using the <strong class="text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA]">Restore Purchases</strong> option in the App.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">10. Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            The App, including its design, code, interface, text, graphics, logos, and other content, is owned by Dmitry Sinkevich or its licensors and is protected by applicable intellectual-property laws.
          </p>
          <p>
            Natural Earth and GeoNames data remain subject to the respective licenses and terms described in Section 4.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">11. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            The App may rely on services or components provided by Apple, including iOS, LocalAuthentication, MapKit, iCloud, CloudKit, and the App Store.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your use of those Apple services may be subject to Apple’s own terms and privacy policies. We are not responsible for the availability, functionality, or practices of third-party services.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">12. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            The App is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            To the maximum extent permitted by law, Dmitry Sinkevich disclaims all implied warranties, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, non-infringement, and uninterrupted operation.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not warrant that the App will be error-free, secure, uninterrupted, compatible with every device, or that travel calculations, maps, borders, or geographic data will be accurate or complete.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">13. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Dmitry Sinkevich shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, including loss of data, loss of profits, loss of goodwill, or business interruption, arising from or related to your use of the App.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            In no event shall our total liability arising from or relating to the App exceed the amount you paid for the App or its in-app purchases during the 12 months before the claim arose, or USD 10 if you made no paid purchase.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations of liability, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">14. Termination</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            We may suspend or terminate your access to the App if you materially breach these Terms or use the App in a manner that creates legal or security risk.
          </p>
          <p>
            Upon termination, the license granted to you ends. Sections concerning intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability, and governing law survive termination.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#221F2C] dark:text-[#F5F3FA] mb-3">15. Changes to These Terms</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            We may update these Terms from time to time. The “Effective Date” above shows when the current version took effect.
          </p>
          <p>
            If changes are material, we may provide notice within the App or through an updated App Store listing. Continued use of the App after changes take effect means you accept the updated Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
